# Normalize line endings in the repository, matching .editorconfig.
#
# .editorconfig already declares `end_of_line = lf` for every file, but
# .editorconfig only configures editors. Without a .gitattributes file, git
# falls back to each contributor's local `core.autocrlf`, so the same commit
# checks out with different line endings on different machines. That made
# `pnpm run format:check` fail on every formatter-owned file for anyone with
# `core.autocrlf=true` (Windows) while passing on CI, which runs on ubuntu.
#
# `* text=auto eol=lf` normalizes to LF in the repository and checks out LF
# everywhere, regardless of the contributor's git configuration. Committed
# bytes are therefore identical across platforms.
#
# This does not touch the research dataset's content: `data/ilocano-
# synthetic-data.json` is already stored with LF endings in git, so its
# committed bytes and its SHA-256 are unchanged. Verified, not assumed.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets must never be line-ending normalized or corrupted.
*.ico binary
